Abstract = {The research papers assembled in this West European Politics issue are
   placed in an encompassing framework specifying components of the
   electoral and party studies research area. This makes it possible to
   identify complementarities, conflicts, and empty spaces left by the
   papers. Especially the conditioning of individual party preference
   through the structure of partisan alternatives needs more work.
   Generally analysis of the interaction of micro- and macro-level
   mechanisms impinging on the vote choice is called for.},
