Number = {3, SI},
Pages = {403-424},
Abstract = {This article considers individual, communal, and cantonal sources of
   voting behavior in the 2007 National Council elections in Switzerland.
   Using hierarchical linear models, it is shown how the vote propensity
   for the jive main parties (CVP, FDP, Greens, SP, and SVP) varies across
   individuals, communes, and cantons. Key explanatory factors at each of
   these levels are explored, as well as cross-party differences in the
